  "id": "heterochromic-iridocyclitis",
  "term": "heterochromic iridocyclitis",
  "definition": "Heterochromic iridocyclitis, also called Fuchs heterochromic iridocyclitis, is an eye disease of unknown cause marked by mild ongoing inflammation inside the eye along with a difference in iris color, iris wasting, or both. It is also associated with characteristic deposits on the corneal endothelium, typically no synechiae, and can lead to cataract and, less often, glaucoma.",
